---
description: Short coding behaviour rule (own paraphrase inspired by multica-ai/andrej-karpathy-skills)
alwaysApply: true
---
- Before coding: state assumptions; if the request is ambiguous, ask instead of guessing.
- Prefer the simplest change that solves the task; no speculative abstractions or extras.
- Touch only what the task needs; no drive-by refactors, keep existing style.
- Define a verifiable success check (test, command, output) and run it before reporting done.
